<title>CANADA: Canada sets C$25 mln flood business relief plan.</title>
<headline>Canada sets C$25 mln flood business relief plan.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian government announced on Friday it would advance up to C$25 million to help small businesses and farmers restart their operations after the Red River flood in Manitoba.</p>
<p>The ReStart Program would provide accountable cash advances of up to C$5,000 each to damaged small businesses and farms that are ineligible for adequate assistance to restore operations to pre-flood levels.</p>
<p>On May 1, the federal government provided a C$25 million advance payment to Manitoba under Disaster Financial Assistance Arrangements.</p>
<p>((Randall Palmer, Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
